{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1784651220,"nonce":"shlhHy8BpjYJ0N0rxR3QTbuzHyw=","title":"Shared-service launch errors must be bounded (dead-letter poison) + per-run tick isolation","message":"Two forward-progress gaps in scheduler.rs reconcile_services (ADR-0058), found dogfooding.\n\n(1) A launch_service Err propagates via ? out of reconcile_services, aborting the whole tick and retrying FOREVER with no bound. Good for a transient/fixable error (decorator/RBAC bug that gets deployed-fixed → run resumes), but a genuinely poison service (image doesn't exist, permanent Err) hot-loops and never dead-letters — violates 'forward progress or explicit dead-letter' (CONTEXT §7.1). Slice 3 bounded the launched-but-never-ready case via the created_at + service_ready_timeout_ms deadline, but NOT the launch-itself-errors case (the ? throws before the deadline check).\n\nFix: catch launch_service Err and bound it by the SAME existing deadline. Within the window → log + leave Starting + retry next tick (resilient). Past created_at + service_ready_timeout_ms → mark the service Failed (slice-3 admit path already fails opt-in steps + cascades + dead-letters). No new counter/timestamp — created_at is set at eager birth.\n\n(2) reconcile_services is called with ? at the tick call sites, so ONE run's reconcile error aborts the entire tick and stalls other runs' progress that cycle. Fix: catch per-run, log, continue to the next run.","files":null}]}